  "description": "The field prosthetic arm uses simple joints and mechanical linkages that a sietch workshop can assemble. Field prosthetics research opens production at the precision workshop; each limb consumes forty steel and four industrial components and requires Crafting 5.\n\nA surgeon must fit the physical part using medicine. The replacement remains less capable than a natural arm, and installation still carries the usual surgical risk. This artwork depicts the carried replacement part; it adds no new pawn-body rendering.",
